(1976263, 270438, 33515, '<td valign="top">Seems to be a better example of Bokeh the Shallow DOF.  5</td>', 'Seems to be a better example of Bokeh the Shallow DOF.  5', '2005-12-24 20:13:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976265, 271317, 33515, '<td valign="top">Seems to be a better example of Bokeh the Shallow DOF.  5</td>', 'Seems to be a better example of Bokeh the Shallow DOF.  5', '2005-12-24 20:14:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976267, 270238, 33515, '<td valign="top">Seems to be a better example of Bokeh the Shallow DOF.  5</td>', 'Seems to be a better example of Bokeh the Shallow DOF.  5', '2005-12-24 20:14:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976318, 271246, 37015, '<td valign="top">Although this perfectly meets the challenge - great DOF, nice, crisp colors - the focal point is a bit bland.</td>', 'Although this perfectly meets the challenge - great DOF, nice, crisp colors - the focal point is a bit bland.', '2005-12-24 21:06:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976320, 269110, 45414, '<td valign="top">Beautiful picture but lacking SDF</td>', 'Beautiful picture but lacking SDF', '2005-12-24 21:07:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976491, 270505, 41091, '<td valign="top">Hi how did you light this?</td>', 'Hi how did you light this?', '2005-12-24 23:45:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976496, 270680, 32602, '<td valign="top">stunning!!  hairbrush?<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-12-28 21:46:11.</i></td>', 'stunning!!  hairbrush?', '2005-12-24 23:50:20.000000', '2005-12-28 21:46:11.000000', 1),
(1976502, 269311, 33515, '<td valign="top">Even with the focus on the shaded flower the light over powers that and draws my eye to the lit flower.</td>', 'Even with the focus on the shaded flower the light over powers that and draws my eye to the lit flower.', '2005-12-24 23:54:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976620, 270053, 50075, '<td valign="top">I work with computers on a daily basis. I saw this and just about fell off my chair laughing. I like it. Thank you. :)</td>', 'I work with computers on a daily basis. I saw this and just about fell off my chair laughing. I like it. Thank you. :)', '2005-12-25 02:08:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976645, 271026, 25355, '<td valign="top">Lovely shot, the best flower shot I''ve seen so far in this challenge.</td>', 'Lovely shot, the best flower shot I''ve seen so far in this challenge.', '2005-12-25 02:55:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976646, 271272, 25355, '<td valign="top">I''ll reiterate what others have probably said. The depth of field is not very shallow.</td>', 'I''ll reiterate what others have probably said. The depth of field is not very shallow.', '2005-12-25 02:56:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976658, 270505, 37015, '<td valign="top">DOF is not very apparent in this picture.  The high contrast between the background and the flower makes it look almost artificial.  I think if a shadow would''ve been cast on the background as well or there was something to show that the background wasn''t just a void of blackness, it would''ve helped it a bit.</td>', 'DOF is not very apparent in this picture.  The high contrast between the background and the flower makes it look almost artificial.  I think if a shadow would''ve been cast on the background as well or there was something to show that the background wasn''t just a void of blackness, it would''ve helped it a bit.', '2005-12-25 03:27:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976660, 271380, 37015, '<td valign="top">I think the DOF is too shallow in this instance - it makes the object look as if it''s just up against a brown backdrop instead of a background that''s out of focus.  However, I do like the composition and the crispness of the "liquid copper".</td>', 'I think the DOF is too shallow in this instance - it makes the object look as if it''s just up against a brown backdrop instead of a background that''s out of focus.  However, I do like the composition and the crispness of the "liquid copper".', '2005-12-25 03:29:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976664, 269968, 37015, '<td valign="top">I don''t find the subject interesting enough to help pull the image together.  Although the DOF is well done, the background and the subject are unrelated so it''s hard for me to feel anything for the image.</td>', 'I don''t find the subject interesting enough to help pull the image together.  Although the DOF is well done, the background and the subject are unrelated so it''s hard for me to feel anything for the image.', '2005-12-25 03:32:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976666, 271314, 37015, '<td valign="top">A slightly more shallow DOF would''ve helped this image quite a bit and would''ve isolated the closest flower more.  However, I like the lighting and composition.</td>', 'A slightly more shallow DOF would''ve helped this image quite a bit and would''ve isolated the closest flower more.  However, I like the lighting and composition.', '2005-12-25 03:34:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976669, 269802, 37015, '<td valign="top">No Rudolph? :P  I really like this picture for some reason.  It''s a very simple subject, but it''s composed very well, the lighting is great, and the DOF is great.</td>', 'No Rudolph? :P  I really like this picture for some reason.  It''s a very simple subject, but it''s composed very well, the lighting is great, and the DOF is great.', '2005-12-25 03:35:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976674, 269856, 37015, '<td valign="top">Although the DOF is "right" in this image, focusing on the middle ornament is quite random.  Since it''s the only one in focus, my attention is drawn to it but then I''m left wondering what the significance of the middle ornament is.  I would''ve liked to see an outtake with her maybe reaching for the middle one or simply looking at it.</td>', 'Although the DOF is "right" in this image, focusing on the middle ornament is quite random.  Since it''s the only one in focus, my attention is drawn to it but then I''m left wondering what the significance of the middle ornament is.  I would''ve liked to see an outtake with her maybe reaching for the middle one or simply looking at it.', '2005-12-25 03:40:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976764, 271038, 45559, '<td valign="top">I should have copyrighted my "Too Late" idea. :P</td>', 'I should have copyrighted my "Too Late" idea. :P', '2005-12-25 08:21:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976765, 269110, 48579, '<td valign="top">How is this Shallow DOF ????</td>', 'How is this Shallow DOF ????', '2005-12-25 08:25:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976789, 270725, 27786, '<td valign="top">I was once told that when taking portraits, the only thing that has to be in focus is the eyes. The rest of the face can be out of focus.<br/> <br/>Just my $0.02</td>', 'I was once told that when taking portraits, the only thing that has to be in focus is the eyes. The rest of the face can be out of focus. Just my $0.02', '2005-12-25 09:20:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976792, 270993, 27786, '<td valign="top">Probably too much jpeg compression, there are many visible artifacts on the picture. It would have scored better if the picture was of a better quality.</td>', 'Probably too much jpeg compression, there are many visible artifacts on the picture. It would have scored better if the picture was of a better quality.', '2005-12-25 09:23:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976793, 270508, 27786, '<td valign="top">You should have used a flash to lighten the Homer up. It''s way too dark with that window behind him.</td>', 'You should have used a flash to lighten the Homer up. It''s way too dark with that window behind him.', '2005-12-25 09:24:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976794, 269424, 27786, '<td valign="top">Great photo!</td>', 'Great photo!', '2005-12-25 09:25:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976795, 270925, 27786, '<td valign="top">Thumbs up!</td>', 'Thumbs up!', '2005-12-25 09:26:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976796, 271272, 27786, '<td valign="top">Kind of missed the shallow DOF.</td>', 'Kind of missed the shallow DOF.', '2005-12-25 09:26:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976869, 271057, 7322, '<td valign="top">This is nice. I think it would be better if you had placed the light so that it wasn''t included in the shot since it distracts from an otherwise very simple composition.</td>', 'This is nice. I think it would be better if you had placed the light so that it wasn''t included in the shot since it distracts from an otherwise very simple composition.', '2005-12-25 12:25:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976870, 270625, 7322, '<td valign="top">It''s not a particularly visually appealing cup, sadly. It''s kind of drab and colorless. I think if you had eliminated the paper insulator it might have been a little better-- I don''t really know what the cup looks like. Perhaps this would be less boring if you could see someone in the background enjoying a cup. All, I can make out is an arm (it took me awhile to figure it out--I thought at first it was a jacket thrown over the chair) and a bit of blue jeans).</td>', 'It''s not a particularly visually appealing cup, sadly. It''s kind of drab and colorless. I think if you had eliminated the paper insulator it might have been a little better-- I don''t really know what the cup looks like. Perhaps this would be less boring if you could see someone in the background enjoying a cup. All, I can make out is an arm (it took me awhile to figure it out--I thought at first it was a jacket thrown over the chair) and a bit of blue jeans).', '2005-12-25 12:27:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976871, 271083, 7322, '<td valign="top">Not super original but it works okay.  I''m a bit distracted by the crumbs from the the pencils being freshly sharpened. I think this would work better with a new set of pencils (although there is a personal quality in that these are regularly used by someone). Maybe if they were set up with some art work in progress or some other well-used artist materials?</td>', 'Not super original but it works okay.  I''m a bit distracted by the crumbs from the the pencils being freshly sharpened. I think this would work better with a new set of pencils (although there is a personal quality in that these are regularly used by someone). Maybe if they were set up with some art work in progress or some other well-used artist materials?', '2005-12-25 12:30:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976878, 270449, 7322, '<td valign="top">It took me a second to find evidence of shallow DOF in this. I actually like this composition quite a bit. I like the panties used as a design element with the unorthodox amount of empty space above (I''m find of this type of composition although I prefer a narrower, more vertical frame when utilizing it). Sadly, I don''t really think shallow DOF does anything to enhance this composition. It actually detracts from the what could be a crisp and clean graphic statement. For this composition to work really well the focus needs to be very crisp and the pink needs to really be separate from the white. I would enjoy seeing this done again with a vertical frame and very sharp focus, no shadows,and a perfectly spotless white background so that it appears as one graphic statement.</td>', 'It took me a second to find evidence of shallow DOF in this. I actually like this composition quite a bit. I like the panties used as a design element with the unorthodox amount of empty space above (I''m find of this type of composition although I prefer a narrower, more vertical frame when utilizing it). Sadly, I don''t really think shallow DOF does anything to enhance this composition. It actually detracts from the what could be a crisp and clean graphic statement. For this composition to work really well the focus needs to be very crisp and the pink needs to really be separate from the white. I would enjoy seeing this done again with a vertical frame and very sharp focus, no shadows,and a perfectly spotless white background so that it appears as one graphic statement.', '2005-12-25 12:35:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976882, 271243, 7322, '<td valign="top">This just looks very unappealing. The lighting is very flat (almost looks like flash) and the candy just looks sad and kind of turd-like. I''m sorry to be so blunt but that was my first reaction when I saw this. Food shots are really difficult. It takes a certain kind of lighting and set design expertise (I certainly don''t claim to have any) to make it look appealing on camera. Setting the candy (or cookies?) up on an attractive dish would be a start. Maybe in nice little foil cups? The aluminum foil looks pretty haphazard and adds quite a bit of glare.</td>', 'This just looks very unappealing. The lighting is very flat (almost looks like flash) and the candy just looks sad and kind of turd-like. I''m sorry to be so blunt but that was my first reaction when I saw this. Food shots are really difficult. It takes a certain kind of lighting and set design expertise (I certainly don''t claim to have any) to make it look appealing on camera. Setting the candy (or cookies?) up on an attractive dish would be a start. Maybe in nice little foil cups? The aluminum foil looks pretty haphazard and adds quite a bit of glare.', '2005-12-25 12:40:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976893, 271332, 7322, '<td valign="top">This is very strange and surreal. I think I get how you did it (is that George Washington or Thomas Jefferson?) Very creative. I can''t imagine how most voters will like it (it looks a bit arty for most tastes on this site) but it certainly makes use of shallow DOF (the way I interpret it anyway).  I''m not sure if I like it or am just responding to the unusual quality. It certainly has me thinking about it, anyway which is more than I can say for the majority of DPC offerings. To me, it looks like it would make a cool album cover. I''m still not sure I actually like this image but I''m scoring high for meeting the challenge,and for originallity, creativity, and technical soundness.</td>', 'This is very strange and surreal. I think I get how you did it (is that George Washington or Thomas Jefferson?) Very creative. I can''t imagine how most voters will like it (it looks a bit arty for most tastes on this site) but it certainly makes use of shallow DOF (the way I interpret it anyway).  I''m not sure if I like it or am just responding to the unusual quality. It certainly has me thinking about it, anyway which is more than I can say for the majority of DPC offerings. To me, it looks like it would make a cool album cover. I''m still not sure I actually like this image but I''m scoring high for meeting the challenge,and for originallity, creativity, and technical soundness.', '2005-12-25 12:46:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976894, 271254, 7322, '<td valign="top">Cute. I''d like to see a less shiny surface and I''d like a seamless background.</td>', 'Cute. I''d like to see a less shiny surface and I''d like a seamless background.', '2005-12-25 12:47:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976902, 271339, 7322, '<td valign="top">Very striking. I''m wondering how many people are going to interpret this as creative use of shallow DOF.<br/>I don''t profess to have a lot of technical know-how but this seems more like creative use of high contrast and high key lighting. I guess to achieve this fading into whiteness effect you had to start by blurring the subject a bit? But couldn''t that also be the result of really extreme highlighting?  I really like the photo quite a bit. I just am not getting shallow DOF from it. The bangs look a bit blurred in the front but I feel like I''m grasping to make this meet the challenge. I''m guessing you are going to get plenty of high votes from people who don''t mind shoehorning a photo  to fit a challenge if they really like the shot. I''m not really sure how to vote on this.</td>', 'Very striking. I''m wondering how many people are going to interpret this as creative use of shallow DOF.I don''t profess to have a lot of technical know-how but this seems more like creative use of high contrast and high key lighting. I guess to achieve this fading into whiteness effect you had to start by blurring the subject a bit? But couldn''t that also be the result of really extreme highlighting?  I really like the photo quite a bit. I just am not getting shallow DOF from it. The bangs look a bit blurred in the front but I feel like I''m grasping to make this meet the challenge. I''m guessing you are going to get plenty of high votes from people who don''t mind shoehorning a photo  to fit a challenge if they really like the shot. I''m not really sure how to vote on this.', '2005-12-25 12:54:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976904, 271038, 7322, '<td valign="top">A nice idea. It seems a bit overexposed.</td>', 'A nice idea. It seems a bit overexposed.', '2005-12-25 12:55:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976906, 270998, 7322, '<td valign="top">I like the arrangement. I think it was a mistake to crop off the bottom of the foreground ornament. The background looks a bit grey and dingy to me.</td>', 'I like the arrangement. I think it was a mistake to crop off the bottom of the foreground ornament. The background looks a bit grey and dingy to me.', '2005-12-25 12:56:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976907, 270885, 7322, '<td valign="top">I don''t understand the inclusion of the wall in the upper right corner of the frame. It appears to be the sharpest part of this image. This angle is a bit extreme for this type of object. This is all just too monochromatic.</td>', 'I don''t understand the inclusion of the wall in the upper right corner of the frame. It appears to be the sharpest part of this image. This angle is a bit extreme for this type of object. This is all just too monochromatic.', '2005-12-25 12:59:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976910, 270650, 7322, '<td valign="top">This looks kind of messy and cluttered with the frayed ribbon,the loop, and the silver glitter on the ornament. The greyish blurred bacgkround doesn''t do much to enhance this object. It just sort of looks like a blue, sort of glittery lump with a phallus protruding from the middle. I find it weirdly unpleasant. Sorry.</td>', 'This looks kind of messy and cluttered with the frayed ribbon,the loop, and the silver glitter on the ornament. The greyish blurred bacgkround doesn''t do much to enhance this object. It just sort of looks like a blue, sort of glittery lump with a phallus protruding from the middle. I find it weirdly unpleasant. Sorry.', '2005-12-25 13:03:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976911, 271149, 7322, '<td valign="top">Nice colors and interesting abstraction of line and form created from the areas of sharp and soft focus. I don''t love it but I appreciate it.</td>', 'Nice colors and interesting abstraction of line and form created from the areas of sharp and soft focus. I don''t love it but I appreciate it.', '2005-12-25 13:05:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976912, 270866, 7322, '<td valign="top">I''m only seeing one bee in this shot...My eye goes to the buds first and then the bee. Maybe if there was closer focus on the bee?</td>', 'I''m only seeing one bee in this shot...My eye goes to the buds first and then the bee. Maybe if there was closer focus on the bee?', '2005-12-25 13:07:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976926, 271271, 7322, '<td valign="top">This must have taken a few takes. This is one of those shots where I can''t imagine it anywhere outside a challenge.  Without the title I would think,"Huh? Why photograph this?"  I like a photo to make some kind of statement, be it visual, emotional ,or informational, and this just doesn''t do any of those things. I can''t fault the technical aspects.</td>', 'This must have taken a few takes. This is one of those shots where I can''t imagine it anywhere outside a challenge.  Without the title I would think,"Huh? Why photograph this?"  I like a photo to make some kind of statement, be it visual, emotional ,or informational, and this just doesn''t do any of those things. I can''t fault the technical aspects.', '2005-12-25 13:16:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976927, 271114, 7322, '<td valign="top">This is fine from a technical and compostional standpoint. The subject is very ho-hum for me.</td>', 'This is fine from a technical and compostional standpoint. The subject is very ho-hum for me.', '2005-12-25 13:17:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976929, 270610, 7322, '<td valign="top">It is hard to see what the title is referring to. It takes a second to realize this is a concert hall of some sort. Mostly, I''m seeing the backs of peoples'' heads. I think this might be a case in which it would have been better to focus on the performer(s) and blur the audience. The focal point of this photo seems to be the gentlemen''s rather shiny ear which leads my eye directly to the head of the woman directly in the middle of the lower portion of the frame. Then I see the blurred forms in the background which has taken me the entire time I''ve been writing to figure out that all those blobs of light are a chorus. I thought I was seeing a blurred out chandelier.</td>', 'It is hard to see what the title is referring to. It takes a second to realize this is a concert hall of some sort. Mostly, I''m seeing the backs of peoples'' heads. I think this might be a case in which it would have been better to focus on the performer(s) and blur the audience. The focal point of this photo seems to be the gentlemen''s rather shiny ear which leads my eye directly to the head of the woman directly in the middle of the lower portion of the frame. Then I see the blurred forms in the background which has taken me the entire time I''ve been writing to figure out that all those blobs of light are a chorus. I thought I was seeing a blurred out chandelier.', '2005-12-25 13:23:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976931, 271258, 7322, '<td valign="top">I think a closer and  lower angle of view would improve this. I don''t care for the shine and the blue cast to the foreground.</td>', 'I think a closer and  lower angle of view would improve this. I don''t care for the shine and the blue cast to the foreground.', '2005-12-25 13:26:02.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(1976940, 271038, 7743, '<td valign="top">This is a good idea though I think slightly more dof is needed to show more detail in the woman in the background.</td>', 'This is a good idea though I think slightly more dof is needed to show more detail in the woman in the background.', '2005-12-25 13:41:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976943, 269273, 7743, '<td valign="top">Great pattern from the chains and the sparkle however I think this may have worked better in a vertical format to emphasize the linear aspect of the chains.</td>', 'Great pattern from the chains and the sparkle however I think this may have worked better in a vertical format to emphasize the linear aspect of the chains.', '2005-12-25 13:43:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(1976988, 269211, 30896, '<td valign="top">I guess it would be much better without the wrapping - now it seems to spoil otherwise beautiful contrast of the reflection and the background</td>', 'I guess it would be much better without the wrapping - now it seems to spoil otherwise beautiful contrast of the reflection and the background', '2005-12-25 14:48:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(1977070, 270638, 44743, '<td valign="top">I thought it was a wonderful picture even before I noticed that the focus was on "Who let the Dogs Out".  Nicely done.</td>', 'I thought it was a wonderful picture even before I noticed that the focus was on "Who let the Dogs Out".  Nicely done.', '2005-12-25 16:16:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(1977073, 269334, 44743, '<td valign="top">One of my favorite pictures.  Love the endless pattern of spools.  Great colors.</td>', 'One of my favorite pictures.  Love the endless pattern of spools.  Great colors.', '2005-12-25 16:19:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(1977075, 271324, 44743, '<td valign="top">This is one of my favorites!  Perfect DOF!</td>', 'This is one of my favorites!  Perfect DOF!', '2005-12-25 16:23:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1977076, 269260, 44743, '<td valign="top">Fantastic!  How did you ever manage to catch that drop?  Beautifully done.</td>', 'Fantastic!  How did you ever manage to catch that drop?  Beautifully done.', '2005-12-25 16:25:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(1977096, 270889, 49773, '<td valign="top">...creative...nice composition...</td>', '...creative...nice composition...', '2005-12-25 16:57:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(1977111, 269943, 30364, '<td valign="top">An elegant idea, effectively executed.  The depth of field nicely isolates the subject, but there''s also something appealing about the inverted fan shape of the out-of-focus background material.  7.</td>', 'An elegant idea, effectively executed.  The depth of field nicely isolates the subject, but there''s also something appealing about the inverted fan shape of the out-of-focus background material.  7.', '2005-12-25 17:23:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(1977150, 269387, 49773, '<td valign="top">nice idea, it would be better if the model framed himself with the fingers, this way he''s hiding the face...</td>', 'nice idea, it would be better if the model framed himself with the fingers, this way he''s hiding the face...', '2005-12-25 18:34:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(1977156, 271109, 15330, '<td valign="top">Love the colors.</td>', 'Love the colors.', '2005-12-25 18:47:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(1977160, 270716, 49997, '<td valign="top">nice little kitty. unfortunately a total photoshop edit i think as one can see the edges was darkened to create the DOF, maybee a little bit of dof on the pinky. sorry</td>', 'nice little kitty. unfortunately a total photoshop edit i think as one can see the edges was darkened to create the DOF, maybee a little bit of dof on the pinky. sorry', '2005-12-25 18:48:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(1977162, 271110, 15330, '<td valign="top">Nice detail, and correct exposure for the squirel, I know how hard it is to get the right exposure when there is snow in the scene. There is too much dead space in the top half of the photo, a tighter crop might help.</td>', 'Nice detail, and correct exposure for the squirel, I know how hard it is to get the right exposure when there is snow in the scene. There is too much dead space in the top half of the photo, a tighter crop might help.', '2005-12-25 18:50:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(1977166, 271334, 50093, '<td valign="top">cool picture</td>', 'cool picture', '2005-12-25 18:53:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(1977198, 271237, 49716, '<td valign="top">Was this shallow DOF or Gaussian Blur?</td>', 'Was this shallow DOF or Gaussian Blur?', '2005-12-25 19:32:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(1977208, 271373, 50094, '<td valign="top">this is a great example of shallow depth of field...and capturing the reflection in the ball add some depth back to the picture</td>', 'this is a great example of shallow depth of field...and capturing the reflection in the ball add some depth back to the picture', '2005-12-25 19:43:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(1977211, 270778, 50094, '<td valign="top">this is photo is a little to busy for shallow depth of field...it almost seems like a blurred motion</td>', 'this is photo is a little to busy for shallow depth of field...it almost seems like a blurred motion', '2005-12-25 19:45:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1977212, 270688, 50094, '<td valign="top">Having the front ball be in focus would help the composition greatly</td>', 'Having the front ball be in focus would help the composition greatly', '2005-12-25 19:45:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(1977214, 270876, 50094, '<td valign="top">very nice use of shallow dof to focus on the main area...would be nicer if it started to blue right after the silver plate</td>', 'very nice use of shallow dof to focus on the main area...would be nicer if it started to blue right after the silver plate', '2005-12-25 19:46:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(1977216, 271380, 50094, '<td valign="top">not enough contrast between the foreground and background to tell that it is shallow dof</td>', 'not enough contrast between the foreground and background to tell that it is shallow dof', '2005-12-25 19:47:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(1977217, 269728, 50094, '<td valign="top">the lights distract from the glass</td>', 'the lights distract from the glass', '2005-12-25 19:47:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1977219, 270598, 50094, '<td valign="top">the effect of the shallow dof could have been pushed more to create a more dramatic picture</td>', 'the effect of the shallow dof could have been pushed more to create a more dramatic picture', '2005-12-25 19:48:25.000000', NULL, 1),
