(1984027, 270621, 15266, '<td valign="top">I scored your shot a 6, I thought the light and DOF were very well handled.  Congrats on your first challenge and a very respectable first score.  Good luck in the future.</td>', 'I scored your shot a 6, I thought the light and DOF were very well handled.  Congrats on your first challenge and a very respectable first score.  Good luck in the future.', '2005-12-28 14:02:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(1984034, 270621, 25728, '<td valign="top">Good job with the lighting! Everything is nice and evenly lit, and that is really hard to do - especially with something sparkly that has lights behind it! <br/></td>', 'Good job with the lighting! Everything is nice and evenly lit, and that is really hard to do - especially with something sparkly that has lights behind it! ', '2005-12-28 14:04:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(1984040, 270621, 29490, '<td valign="top">I was a 5-er.  If the noise in the bg been eliminated I would have bumped up.  Overall I agree with id, good handling of dof and lighting.  Very respectable first entry indeed - I look forward to seeing your future entries!</td>', 'I was a 5-er.  If the noise in the bg been eliminated I would have bumped up.  Overall I agree with id, good handling of dof and lighting.  Very respectable first entry indeed - I look forward to seeing your future entries!', '2005-12-28 14:05:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(1984042, 270621, 6519, '<td valign="top">You did a good job having sharp focus on the eyes. The background colors work well with the statue.<br/>On the down side, a shot of a little statue isn''t all that exciting.<br/>It would help if your horizon was straight.<br/>Good first try, Joyah!<br/></td>', 'You did a good job having sharp focus on the eyes. The background colors work well with the statue.On the down side, a shot of a little statue isn''t all that exciting.It would help if your horizon was straight.Good first try, Joyah!', '2005-12-28 14:06:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(1984060, 271227, 93, '<td valign="top">I don''t know why this scored so low.. but I have my theories..<br/> <br/>1: Too dark.  I don''t think a lot of people have their monitors calibrated properly, but that''s a danger with any darker image you submit here.  Were it advanced editing, I could have done things to improve this.<br/> <br/>2: Lack of true focal point.  The hand is my focal point, which was designed to grab you, then let you wander off up into the fading face and empty eyes.. (which worked for some of you.. woo hoo!).  However, because of the lack of advanced editing, I had to do edits which degraded the color quality, and had to use a blur method which took the sharp focus off the fist, making it seem fuzzy too.  Le sigh.<br/> <br/>3: Scary factor.  I had comments that it was *too* creepy.  I love that on DPC, you get penalized for doing your job too well.<br/> <br/>4: Misunderstanding of Challenge.  I''m still convinced that far too many people have no idea what Shallow DOF really *IS*..  Look at the blue ribbon winner.  That''s not really Shallow DOF.  Sure, the background is completely out of focus, but the main subject is entirely *in* focus.  The background could have been 3 miles away, we don''t know.  Anyway, this theory is last because it''s the least strong.  I''m sure I got hit for it, but not as badly as I thought at first.<br/> <br/>Thanks everyone for some wonderful comments.  This is currently my best ever lower scoring challenge photo.</td>', 'I don''t know why this scored so low.. but I have my theories.. 1: Too dark.  I don''t think a lot of people have their monitors calibrated properly, but that''s a danger with any darker image you submit here.  Were it advanced editing, I could have done things to improve this. 2: Lack of true focal point.  The hand is my focal point, which was designed to grab you, then let you wander off up into the fading face and empty eyes.. (which worked for some of you.. woo hoo!).  However, because of the lack of advanced editing, I had to do edits which degraded the color quality, and had to use a blur method which took the sharp focus off the fist, making it seem fuzzy too.  Le sigh. 3: Scary factor.  I had comments that it was *too* creepy.  I love that on DPC, you get penalized for doing your job too well. 4: Misunderstanding of Challenge.  I''m still convinced that far too many people have no idea what Shallow DOF really *IS*..  Look at the blue ribbon winner.  That''s not really Shallow DOF.  Sure, the background is completely out of focus, but the main subject is entirely *in* focus.  The background could have been 3 miles away, we don''t know.  Anyway, this theory is last because it''s the least strong.  I''m sure I got hit for it, but not as badly as I thought at first. Thanks everyone for some wonderful comments.  This is currently my best ever lower scoring challenge photo.', '2005-12-28 14:11:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(1984063, 270621, 22970, '<td valign="top">I think you did a good job on the shallow dof. The background colors look good with the image. This is my opinion but what I think brought down your score was the tilted base of the statue and the fact that the statue is not a ''wow'' subject. It is beautiful and I think you did a good job with the broken background. I wish you the best and more comments in the future.<br/>SE</td>', 'I think you did a good job on the shallow dof. The background colors look good with the image. This is my opinion but what I think brought down your score was the tilted base of the statue and the fact that the statue is not a ''wow'' subject. It is beautiful and I think you did a good job with the broken background. I wish you the best and more comments in the future.SE', '2005-12-28 14:12:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(1984066, 270621, 811, '<td valign="top">Overall, I think you met the challenge well -- it does have shallow depth of field.  You also have some nice bokeh patterns in the back.<br/> <br/>From my experience, pictures of figurines do not do as well on dpc.  That said, I think you could have made this more interesting by chosing a unique angle, or including just part of the fairy in the picture (not the whole thing).  As one photographer told me.  Frame your shot, then get closer.  Repeat. ;)  Don''t be afraid to fill the frame with your subject.</td>', 'Overall, I think you met the challenge well -- it does have shallow depth of field.  You also have some nice bokeh patterns in the back. From my experience, pictures of figurines do not do as well on dpc.  That said, I think you could have made this more interesting by chosing a unique angle, or including just part of the fairy in the picture (not the whole thing).  As one photographer told me.  Frame your shot, then get closer.  Repeat. ;)  Don''t be afraid to fill the frame with your subject.', '2005-12-28 14:14:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(1984076, 270621, 18450, '<td valign="top">Very good first entry Joyah. Your focus on the statue is excellent, choice of dof great. Lighting works well for this shot. If you''d cropped off the base of the statue it would have helped I think as I feel the fairy is straight, just the angle of the base. <br/> <br/>Good work, looking forward to seeing more of your images<br/> <br/>sue</td>', 'Very good first entry Joyah. Your focus on the statue is excellent, choice of dof great. Lighting works well for this shot. If you''d cropped off the base of the statue it would have helped I think as I feel the fairy is straight, just the angle of the base.  Good work, looking forward to seeing more of your images sue', '2005-12-28 14:19:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(1984089, 270621, 45524, '<td valign="top">I was a 6 voter, I found if the object had been a little sharper on focus, it would have score better, also instead of straight on lighting(or flash) that a side light would have made a more dramatic shot, perhaps light from the front and shoot from a side angle. also more of the frame with the object. Overall good job on your first challenge.</td>', 'I was a 6 voter, I found if the object had been a little sharper on focus, it would have score better, also instead of straight on lighting(or flash) that a side light would have made a more dramatic shot, perhaps light from the front and shoot from a side angle. also more of the frame with the object. Overall good job on your first challenge.', '2005-12-28 14:23:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(1984129, 270621, 13719, '<td valign="top">I missed the voting for this one, I would have given it a 6 very good job with focusing on the eyes. <br/>One thing I noticed, it would have been better if the horizon was straight maybe a little more background space around your statue or maybe other statues behind like this one with more background space them.<br/> <br/>Good try on your first contest Joyah<br/></td>', 'I missed the voting for this one, I would have given it a 6 very good job with focusing on the eyes. One thing I noticed, it would have been better if the horizon was straight maybe a little more background space around your statue or maybe other statues behind like this one with more background space them. Good try on your first contest Joyah', '2005-12-28 14:34:06.000000', NULL, 0),
